{"kind":"request","text":"Decide three E4 compatibility seams before source implementation. Root and peer read act-environment sections7/12/15 and current7bb C3 source. The source-only plan is /private/tmp/artroom-e4-precode-plan-questions-20261115.md; no E4 code or runtime has changed.\n\n1. Version.id is authored-act digest (§7.1), while unchanged C3 A→B→A witness (scope-client.test.ts161–182) requires three gesture signings and only latest-live reuse (scope-client.ts389–403). May append-only gesture occurrences repeat the same act digest? Proposal: retain an occurrence position for signing audit, preserve Source.version=actVersion(act), and give third A its own gesture deadline without reusing first A's envelope. Do not add time to the act digest or treat same digest as permission for same-version timer re-enveloping.\n\n2. Authorization.descriptor must stay fixed at first submit (§7.1), but no environment descriptor producer/type or digest exists in current C3 options. What supplies that digest before E6? Proposal: require an explicit descriptor Digest at the E4 boundary and retain it unchanged, leaving construction to its owning step. Please decide the compatibility value for the unchanged C3 seam. Root will not substitute the definition pin or invent a descriptor hash scheme.\n\n3. Existing C1/C3 custody signings have no authorization history, and unchanged C3 witnesses deliberately create originals with ordinary Custody.keep. How should invariant8 classify those? Proposal: keep them as legacy D12 custody, reconcile and resend only existing live bytes, never fabricate past gestures/descriptor/cancellation. A fresh member gesture retains E4 authorization before any new signature. Check invariant8 on E4-created signings and report legacy originals separately. Accept this boundary or specify an explicit cutover.\n\nImplementation will preserve one atomic owner/scope batch retention, not mistake store.exclusive for rollback. A separate authorization namespace unde